{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.95,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U10", "U11"],
      "pins": ["U10.5", "U11.5", "U10.4", "U11.4", "U10.8", "U11.8"],
      "nets": ["GND", "5V_switched_CAN"],
      "observed": "U10 pin 5 (GND2) and U11 pin 5 (GND2) are connected to the same GND net as U10 pin 4 (GND1) and U11 pin 4 (GND1). Also VCC2 pins (U10.8, U11.8) are on 5V_switched_CAN, which is derived from the non-isolated +5V rail.",
      "expected": "Isolated CAN transceivers require the bus-side ground (GND2) and power (VCC2) to be galvanically isolated from the logic-side ground (GND1) and power. The specification describes 'two isolated CAN buses'.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (CAN0, CAN1), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller (U8, U9) through an isolated CAN transceiver (U11/companion)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The galvanic isolation is defeated. Ground loops and common-mode voltages between the rover's logic ground and the motor controllers' ground can damage the transceivers or cause communication errors.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R36"],
      "pins": ["R36.1", "R36.2"],
      "nets": ["VOUTN", "VOUTP"],
      "observed": "R36 has value '24k' but its description says '24Ω' and its MPN is FRC0805J240TSD, which is a 24Ω resistor. The SPICE deck also uses 24k.",
      "expected": "The bleeder resistor across the PoE output (VOUTP/VOUTN) should be 24kΩ as indicated by the value field and SPICE deck. A 24Ω part would draw excessive current.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R36\") (value \"24k\") ... (description \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±100ppm/℃ ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\") ... (field (name \"MPN\") \"FRC0805J240TSD\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R36 VOUTN VOUTP 24k"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the board is assembled using the MPN, a 24Ω resistor will be placed across the high-voltage PoE output, causing excessive power dissipation, possible overheating, and failure. The intended 24k bleeder would not be present.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain two anomalies: the isolated CAN transceivers have their isolated grounds and power tied to the non-isolated system ground/5V, defeating isolation; and R36 has a value/MPN mismatch (24k vs 24Ω) that would cause a wrong bleeder resistor if assembled per MPN."
}

